```

or, as a library:
<%- end -%>

```ruby
require "<%= path %>"

<%= constant %>.greeting("Ada") # => "Hello, Ada!"
```

## Development

`bin/setup` installs the gems at `Gemfile.lock`'s versions (its first run writes the lock); then
`bundle exec rake` runs the Ruby checks (RuboCop, Steep, the tests with their coverage gate,
yard-lint) and `bundle exec rake checks` everything CI runs:

```sh
bin/setup
bundle exec rake checks
```

See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for the tools those checks need, how a release is cut and,
in a project just generated, its [first steps](CONTRIBUTING.md#first-steps); and
[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the lint and type policy.

